"She asks if you live around here and does not wait for the answer.",
"She brings something useful: a can opener, batteries, soup.",
"She checks her lipstick in the mirror, smooths the skirt down, and hangs the CLEANING sign back on the hook. \"Out front. Walk normal. Normal, Mo.\"",
"She does not interrupt once. At the end she says \"okay\", and then \"okay\" again, softer, and then she asks if you have eaten.",
"She does the voices from the cartoon she grew up on, all of them, and you do not breathe right for ten minutes. The pipe goes cold on the table between you.",
"She gets her bag back off the pavement and presses {0} into your hand and will not take it back. Two people on the block clap, slowly, like it is a movie.",
"She gives you the carton that survived, and insists.",
"She has a bag of food in foil and Tupperware, and she is already looking for plates.",
"She has a cat that watches the entire time. Not the entire time. The door closes on the cat.",
"She has already seen you today. She will not do it twice.",
"She has {0} parcel(s) with your name on them.",
"She hugs like she means it and lets go like she does not.",
"She hugs you properly, the way people hug at airports.",
"She is already moving. \"CRAZY!\" she says, to the whole block, not to you.",
"She is eating cereal standing up, still in scrubs. \"Twelve hours. A man swallowed a key. Do not ask.\" You do not ask.",
"She is gone before the radiator wakes up, and she has taken one of your good socks, which is a choice.",
"She is gone before your arm comes back. The whole block heard her.",
"She is not angry. That is the part that stays with you.",
"She is not offering that tonight.",
"She is on the bed with a cigarette, looking at the ceiling like it owes her money.",
"She is reading, glasses on, one eyebrow up at you over them. \"You ate today? Real food?\"",
"She is sideways on the couch with her feet in your lap before you sit all the way down. \"Hi.\"",
"She is somewhere else entirely, smiling at a streetlight. Business is done here.",
"She is still hurt. She is also still here. Dating can resume.",
"She is talking to you again.",
"She is your girlfriend.",
"She is {0} day{1} late.",
"She kisses your cheek and fixes your collar while she is there.",
"She kisses your cheek, quick and precise, and that is somehow the best part of your week.",
"She knows about the slip. She does not make a speech. It just counts for less today.",
"She laces her fingers through yours like it has always been that way.",
"She leaves it on the counter with a drawing on the bag.",
"She lives above a laundromat. Everything smells like dryer sheets and decisions.",
"She lives with you.",
"She looks around Unit 3B like it is a museum of a man. She says the radiator is \"a lot.\" The door closes.",
"She looks at her screen, then at you. \"There is a warrant on this. You walked in on your own, so I am going to pretend that counts.\" It does: the warrant is lifted.",
"She looks at the money for a long second. \"This is not an apology. But it is forty dollars.\"",
"She looks at you for a second longer than a nurse looks at a patient. \"Huh,\" she says. \"Okay. The offer stands anyway.\"",
"She looks at your eyes for one second too long and changes the subject.",
"She looks up from the essays. \"Give me two minutes, I am telling a fourteen-year-old his thesis is a vibe, not a thesis.\"",
"She looks you up and down like a menu she is not going to order from today. Then she laughs.",
"She opens the box before she decides whether she is still angry. It is hard to be furious at chocolate. She manages.",
"She opens the door four inches. \"It is too early or too late for you to be at my door, Mo. Text first. Like a person.\"",
"She opens the door in a blanket, squinting. \"You are lucky I like you.\" She steps back to let you in, already heading for the couch.",
"She opens the door with a pen behind her ear and a stack of essays under one arm. \"You. Come in, take your shoes off, do not touch the plant.\"",
"She picks up on the first ring, like she always does, like she has been sitting next to it.",
"She posts back. The block takes her side. You read every reply.",
"She pulls the blanket over both of you and is asleep in a minute. You take longer, because you are listening to her breathe.",
"She puts on a record before she says anything. It is a good record. You do not ask what it is.",
